WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.375
The sign-in baseline is short:
multifactor authentication for everyone,

2
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:06.250
legacy sign-in methods blocked,

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.575
and emergency accounts excluded from
anything that could lock them out.

4
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:15.513
Blocking legacy authentication is also
a mandatory federal cloud baseline.

5
00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:17.887
What matters most is how it's switched on.

6
00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:21.959
Every policy runs in report-only
mode first, for at least a week,

7
00:00:21.959 --> 00:00:25.312
so you can see who would be
blocked before anyone is.

8
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:27.337
Then it's enforced ring by ring,

9
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:30.900
and rolled back by turning it
off, never by deleting it.

10
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.410
That makes the emergency
accounts critical.
